      <p class="text-xs text-warm-400 mt-3">Prices are for basic rental including hairstyling. Makeup, photographer, and premium costume upgrades cost extra. Deposit: 200-500 RMB, refundable on return.</p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-warm-900 mt-10 mb-4">Wearing Qipao</h2>
      <p class="text-warm-600 leading-relaxed">Qipao is straightforward by comparison — it''s essentially a one-piece dress. The key is fit. A well-fitted qipao should be snug but not restrictive, with the side slits reaching no higher than mid-thigh. The mandarin collar sits close to the neck without choking. Rental shops will have you try 2-3 sizes. For custom tailoring in Shanghai''s South Bund Fabric Market, your measurements are taken at the first visit, and you return 3-5 days later for a final fitting. Wear seamless undergarments and bring the shoes you plan to pair with the dress to the fitting.</p>
      <div class="mt-4 bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-4 text-sm">
        <p class="font-semibold text-amber-800 mb-1">⚠️ Common Qipao Mistakes</p>
        <ul class="text-amber-700 space-y-1 ml-0 list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong>Sizing too loose:</strong> A qipao should follow your body's lines. If there's more than 2-3cm of ease at the waist, ask for the next size down. Qipao that gapes at the neck or chest was cut wrong — try a different shop.</li>
          <li><strong>Wrong bra:</strong> Regular bras show straps and create visible lines. A racerback or backless bra, adhesive cups, or a seamless bralette is essential. Many Shanghai tailors include bra consultation during fitting.</li>
          <li><strong>Slit too high for daytime:</strong> Mid-thigh or lower for museum visits and daytime wear; higher slits are for evening events and photoshoots only. When in doubt, ask the shop assistant what's appropriate for your activity.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-warm-800 mt-8 mb-3">Custom Qipao Process: Step-by-Step</h3>
      <ol class="mt-2 space-y-3 text-warm-600 text-sm list-decimal pl-5">
        <li><strong class="text-warm-800">Fabric selection (Day 1, 30-60 min):</strong> Browse the ground-floor fabric stalls at South Bund Fabric Market. Silk crepe de chine (素绉缎) is the classic choice (150-300 RMB/meter); silk brocade (织锦缎) for formal occasions (200-400 RMB/meter). Cotton-linen blends for summer qipaos (80-150 RMB/meter). Bring reference photos.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-warm-800">Measurements (Day 1, 15 min):</strong> The tailor takes 15-20 measurements: neck circumference, shoulder width, bust, underbust, waist, hip, armhole, sleeve length, dress length, and slit height. Stand naturally — don't hold your breath to appear slimmer; the dress won't fit.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-warm-800">First fitting/Day 3-4 (optional, 20 min):</strong> The tailor has assembled the main body. Try it on and mark adjustments with chalk. This step can often be skipped for simple designs, saving one day.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-warm-800">Final fitting (Day 4-7, 30 min):</strong> The finished qipao with frog buttons, piping trim, and lining. Wear your intended shoes and undergarments. Walk, sit, and raise your arms — a well-made qipao moves with you.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="text-xs text-warm-400 mt-3">Custom qipao cost: 500-1,500 RMB total (fabric + labor). Faster turnaround (3 days) costs 20-30% more. Bring cash — most fabric market stalls don't accept foreign cards.</p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-warm-900 mt-10 mb-4">Wearing Tang Suit & Zhongshan Suit</h2>
      <p class="text-warm-600 leading-relaxed">The Tang suit is a jacket-and-stand-collar combination that goes over your own shirt. Most shops provide the jacket; you wear your own trousers. The Zhongshan suit is a full tailored outfit with four patch pockets and a turned-down collar — closer to Western suiting in how it''s worn. Both styles take about 10 minutes to put on and adjust. For custom orders, the tailor will take chest, shoulder, sleeve, and waist measurements. Turnaround in Beijing hutong tailors is typically 2-4 days.</p>
      <div class="mt-4 bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-4 text-sm">
        <p class="font-semibold text-amber-800 mb-1">⚠️ Common Tang Suit Mistakes</p>
        <ul class="text-amber-700 space-y-1 ml-0 list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong>Wearing a collared shirt underneath:</strong> The mandarin collar frames the neck. A crew-neck t-shirt or a traditional stand-collar inner shirt (中式立领衬衫) is the only correct option. Visible shirt collars clash with the clean neckline.</li>
          <li><strong>Wrong trousers:</strong> Pair Tang suits with dark, slim-fit trousers — jeans with rivets or cargo pants break the formal look. For Zhongshan suits, the trousers should match the jacket fabric.</li>
          <li><strong>Sizing like a Western blazer:</strong> Tang suits fit closer to the body with shorter sleeves that end at the wrist bone, not the thumb joint. Shoulder seams should sit exactly on the shoulder edge.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-warm-900 mt-10 mb-4">What to Wear Underneath</h2>
      <p class="text-warm-600 leading-relaxed">For Hanfu: a thin tank top or camisole and fitted shorts or leggings. The rental shop provides the inner garment, but having your own base layer adds comfort, especially in summer. For qipao: seamless underwear is essential — the form-fitting silhouette shows every line. Shapewear is commonly worn by locals. For Tang and Zhongshan suits: a plain crew-neck t-shirt and slim-fit trousers work perfectly. Avoid collared shirts under Tang suits since the mandarin collar already frames the neck.</p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-warm-900 mt-10 mb-4">Etiquette & Tips</h2>
      <p class="text-warm-600 leading-relaxed">Walk carefully in long robes — Hanfu hems can drag, especially on stairs and uneven stone paths common at historical sites. For photoshoots: hold the sleeves gracefully when raising your arms; let the fabric drape naturally. When sitting in qipao, cross your ankles rather than your legs to keep the side slits modest. Most importantly: relax. The shop assistants have dressed thousands of people. They know what looks good, and they want you to have a great experience. A smile and basic "xie xie" (thank you) go a long way.</p>

      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold text-warm-900 mt-10 mb-4">How to Find Hanfu Rental Shops as a Foreigner</h2>
      <p class="text-warm-600 leading-relaxed">Most rental shops operate primarily on Chinese platforms, but that doesn't mean they're inaccessible. Here's how to find and book even without Chinese language skills:</p>
      <div class="mt-4 space-y-3">
        <div class="bg-warm-50 rounded-lg p-4">
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-warm-800 text-sm">Xiaohongshu (RED / 小红书)</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-warm-500 mt-1">Search "城市+汉服体验" (e.g. "西安汉服体验" for Xi'an) to find shops with photo reviews. Many shops list WeChat IDs in their posts — add them and communicate via WeChat translate. PRO TIP: Save 5-10 reference photos before you message a shop. They'll understand what style you want without needing language.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-warm-50 rounded-lg p-4">
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-warm-800 text-sm">Meituan (美团)</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-warm-500 mt-1">Meituan is a super-app for booking services. Search "汉服" in the app — results show prices, review scores, and locations on a map. Book directly through the app for 20-30% off walk-in prices. The app is Chinese-only, but screenshots + Google Lens translate works.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-warm-50 rounded-lg p-4">
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-warm-800 text-sm">Hotel Concierge / Hostel Front Desk</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-warm-500 mt-1">Many hotels in Xi'an, Luoyang, and Hangzhou — especially those near scenic areas — can recommend and book Hanfu rentals for you. This is the easiest route: the concierge handles the booking, the shop knows a foreigner is coming, and there's no deposit confusion.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-warm-400 mt-3">Most shops use WeChat Pay or Alipay. Set up Alipay TourPass before your trip — it links a foreign card and works at 90% of tourist-facing rental shops.</p>
    </div>
